{"step_index":732,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-06T05:29:21Z","input_tokens":4609,"cache_read_tokens":73448,"output_tokens":901,"thinking":"**Analyzing PowerShell Activation**\n\nI've been examining the PowerShell activation process for this project. Specifically, I'm noting the required command sequence: `.\\venv\\Scripts\\activate` followed by `python main_gui.py`. The use of virtual environments is critical here. It seems ensuring proper PowerShell activation is a prerequisite before execution. I am also investigating the issues with Unicode characters.\n\n\n**Addressing Unicode Issues**\n\nI'm now focusing on handling potential UnicodeEncodeErrors, particularly with emoji logging in the console output. PowerShell's behavior with Unicode requires careful attention. I've updated my internal rule (Rule 10) to specifically address this, ensuring I use compatible commands in a PowerShell environment and avoid any reliance on Linux commands that could cause errors. Next, I will plan to update `GEMINI.md` and `README.md` to reflect this new rule.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"# Plan: Enforcing PowerShell Native Tooling Rule\n\n## Goal Description\nThe user noticed that the AI assistant frequently attempts to use Linux-specific terminal commands (like `grep`, `cat`, `ls`) which fail in the Windows PowerShell environment. We need to explicitly add a rule to the system prompt (`GEMINI.md`) to instruct the AI to always use PowerShell-compatible commands or cross-platform Git tools.\n\n## Proposed Changes\n\n### `GEMINI.md`\n#### [MODIFY] GEMINI.md\nWe will update Rule #10 to include a strict mandate against using Linux commands directly in the terminal, forcing the AI to remember its environment.\n\n```markdown\n10. **ENTORNO POWERSHELL Y UNICODE (EMOJIS)**:\n    - Para iniciar el proyecto en Windows PowerShell, siempre usar `.\\venv\\Scripts\\activate` seguido de `python main_gui.py`.\n    - Al hacer prints en consola (stdout) que contengan Emojis (muy usados en los logs de este bot con OCR), tener en cuenta que PowerShell puede arrojar `UnicodeEncodeError`. El logger de la terminal debe manejar esta excepción o forzar el encoding a UTF-8.\n    - **MANDATO PARA LA IA:** El entorno es Windows PowerShell. Tienes PROHIBIDO intentar usar comandos nativos de Linux (`grep`, `cat`, `ls`, `sed`, `awk`). Debes usar comandos nativos de PowerShell (`Get-Content`, `Select-String`, `dir`) o herramientas multiplataforma como `git grep`.\n```\n\n## User Review Required\nNo major risks. This is an instructions-only update.\n\n## Verification Plan\n1. Update the `GEMINI.md` file.\n2. Commit and push to GitHub so the rule is preserved.\n3. The AI's system prompt will re-parse this file in future turns, applying the new constraint.","Description":"Plan to enforce PowerShell native commands in GEMINI.md","TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\Brian\\.gemini\\antigravity-cli\\brain\\dab6a3d4-72ff-45ea-898a-cdc9ce4a7ca1\\plan_powershell_rules.md","toolAction":"Writing powershell rules plan","toolSummary":"Write PowerShell plan"}}]}
